      'NEW — **Cost components**: freight, insurance, duty, clearance, handling, inland, inspection, discount, other. Each component has an amount (in the PO\'s supplier currency) and an **allocation basis**: by value / by volume (CBM) / by weight / flat per line. The basis decides how the component\'s cost gets split across line items. By-volume needs carton dims on every line; by-weight needs per-unit weight. If a basis cannot be applied (e.g. by-volume but no line has carton dims set), the calc silently falls back to by-value and surfaces a warning in the summary panel — no silent miscalculation.',
      'NEW — **Landed cost calculator** runs on every PO edit. Per-line landed cost = unit USD price + allocated cost share per unit. Summary panel shows: goods value USD, cost components USD, total landed USD, total volume CBM, total weight kg, and **container fill %** against the chosen container type (20\' = 33.2 CBM, 40\' = 67.7, 40HQ = 76.4 — industry-standard usable capacity). Fill % goes amber at >90% and rose at >100% so you can spot over-packed POs at a glance.',
