      'Fix (server-side, critical): the `/api/ping` health endpoint was returning HTTP 500 in the packaged app. Root cause — the handler read the app version via `require(\'../../package.json\')`, which resolves correctly in the dev source tree but points at a non-existent path inside the packaged asar (the compiled file lives at dist-electron/main/server/index.js, so `../../package.json` → dist-electron/package.json, which isn\'t bundled). The require threw, and the throw turned the whole ping response into a 500. Switched to `app.getVersion()` — the canonical Electron API that works identically in dev and production.',
      'This one bug caused THREE confusing symptoms you reported, all from the same 500: (1) the connection chip sat permanently amber ("Server hiccup") because the client polls /api/ping every 30s and kept getting 500s; (2) "Run network diagnostic" failed at the "Server reachable" step with "returned 500 on /api/ping — not an Image Studio KH server"; (3) yet "Test connection" SUCCEEDED, because it hits /api/whoami (which doesn\'t read package.json) — that contradiction was the giveaway that only the ping endpoint was broken, not the connection.',
