      'Clarification: "Server exposes 89 channels" reworded to "Full API available ✓". The raw channel count confused people into thinking 89 was a number they had to interpret — it\'s just the size of the server\'s RPC API surface (a "yep, the full API is reachable" sanity check). The exact number is now a hover tooltip for the curious; the visible text just confirms the API is there. Nothing was ever wrong — 89 is the expected count.',
      'Why this slipped through: the dev build (npm run dev) uses the source layout where `../../package.json` resolves fine, so /api/ping worked in testing. Only the packaged DMG hit the broken path. Lesson logged — version reads must always go through app.getVersion(), never a relative package.json require. This was the last such require in the codebase (grep-verified).',
