      'Phase 1 of 3 of the post-audit cleanup: reviewed all 6 `eslint-disable react-hooks/exhaustive-deps` instances in the codebase and confirmed every one is intentional and correct (none hide bugs). Added explanatory comments inline so future readers don\'t spend time wondering whether each one is a smell or a documented decision.',
      'The 6 disables: (1) SearchableSelect.jsx:102 — open-time popover snapshot, already commented; (2) Settings/index.jsx:906 — ServerModePanel mount-once user list fetch, comment added; (3) Settings/index.jsx:1358 — BgModelCachePanel mount-once cache fetch, comment added; (4) ImageWorkspace/index.jsx:86 — re-seed workspace settings on file-change only (NOT on every save), comment added explaining the infinite-loop risk if activeImage were in deps; (5) AIStudio/index.jsx:137 — mount-once data kickoff, comment added; (6) Inspector.jsx:46 — NumberInput re-sync on `value` change only (omitting `fmt` because it\'s a new closure every render → infinite loop if listed), comment added.',
      'Pattern across all of them: when an effect captures a function or object that\'s recreated every render, listing it in the dep array creates an infinite loop (effect runs → state changes → re-render → new closure → effect runs again). The `eslint-disable` is the React-recommended escape hatch for exactly this case. The comments now make that clear at each site.',
