      'Clarification: Settings → AI Generation → "Background removal engine" hint now spells out the actual data flow in client mode — "Both options run ON THIS MAC. Local uses the @imgly WASM model on your CPU. remove.bg calls the cloud API directly from this Mac with your own API key. The server is NOT a middleman either way." Because users were unsure whether bg-removal in client mode went through the server (it doesn\'t). Standalone/server mode keeps the original shorter hint.',
      'Why this matters: bg removal is CPU-heavy; users seeing it run slow on an older client Mac were assuming "the server is slow" when in fact the ML inference is just CPU-bound on their own machine. Now the hint tells them that.',
