      'Fix: client mode no longer shows "v0.0.0" in the sidebar footer. Root cause was a routing bug — `app:getVersion` and `app:getPlatform` were registered as PROXIED channels in client mode, meaning the client RPC\'d the server to ask "what version are you?" on every launch. When the server was unreachable during bootstrap (freshly-configured client, wrong URL, server still booting, DHCP-IP-changed, etc.), the RPC failed → bootstrap rejected → `appVersion` stayed at its initial empty value → sidebar fell back to the `v0.0.0` placeholder. Both calls are now LOCAL handlers in client mode, exactly like in standalone / server mode — the version is baked into the bundle, so the client always knows it.',
      'Hardening: the bootstrap sequence in the store now uses `Promise.allSettled` instead of `Promise.all` for the four initial slice calls (version, platform, active company, settings). Pre-fix, one slow / failing call would reject the whole `Promise.all` and silently lose all four values. With allSettled, each slice has an independent fate — a failed settings RPC doesn\'t nuke the version display anymore. Belt-and-braces on top of the routing fix.',
