      'New: collapsible sidebar. Small chevron button at the top-right of the brand row toggles between expanded (220px, text labels visible) and collapsed (~56px, icons only). Gains you about 164px of horizontal real estate when running the app on a smaller display or side-by-side window. Click the chevron again to expand.',
      'Why this also fixes the header-overflow you flagged: with the sidebar at 56px instead of 220px, every page\'s action toolbar has 164px more breathing room to lay out across one row instead of wrapping. Library, AI Studio, Export Center, Overlay Studio — all of them benefit at narrower window sizes. No need for per-page responsive tweaks; the sidebar collapse cascades through.',
      'Collapsed-state behaviour: all nav items, company switcher, footer items show their ICON only — text labels hide via CSS `display:none`. Tooltips on every button (`title` attribute) were already there for keyboard shortcut hints, so hovering each icon still tells you what it does without the visible label. Active-page highlight + connection-state colour dot all still work.',
