      'Fix: every numeric input in the Overlay Studio Inspector — font Size, X / Y position, Width / Height, Rotation, background Padding, background Corner radius — fought you while you tried to type. Clear the Size field to enter "120" and you\'d watch it snap to 8 (the min clamp), then 81, then 812, then 400 (max clamp). Same root cause as the canvas-dimension bug from v0.22.17: parent state immediately re-rendered with the clamped value, overwriting your half-typed text on every keystroke.',
      'Fix: built a shared `NumberInput` component used by all the Inspector numeric fields. It holds a LOCAL string buffer so the input shows exactly what you typed (including empty), and commits to the parent state only on blur, Enter, or Esc. Esc reverts to the last committed value if you change your mind mid-edit.',
      'Resyncs from the underlying value when you\'re NOT editing — so dragging an element on the canvas still updates X/Y/Width/Height in the Inspector instantly. Undo / template-switch updates also flow through correctly. The block only kicks in while you\'re actively typing.',
      'Caller-supplied clamp: each field still has its bounds enforced (font size 8..400, padding 0..200, rotation normalised to -180..180, etc.) — but the clamp runs at COMMIT time, not on every keystroke. Type 9999 → on blur it shows 400.',
      'Behaviour change worth knowing: changes to numeric fields no longer apply live as you type. They apply when you Tab out, press Enter, or click somewhere else. This matches every native macOS form field — text inputs commit on commit, not on each keystroke — and the value you see is always the value the template has. The text field is the one place the live-as-you-type model was actively harmful.',
