      'Fix: conflict detection (v0.17.2) was silently broken on the main Mac for all desktop saves. Symptom: editing a product that had been updated by someone else (or another instance) showed a raw red toast containing "Error invoking remote method \'products:update\': Error: CONFLICT|{...JSON...}" instead of the friendly "Refresh / Overwrite / Cancel" conflict dialog.',
      'Root cause: `parseConflictError(err)` checked `err.message.startsWith(\'CONFLICT|\')`, but Electron\'s `ipcRenderer.invoke` wraps every thrown handler error as `Error invoking remote method \'<channel>\': Error: <original>`. So the sentinel arrived embedded mid-string, the startsWith check returned false, the parse fell through to null, the catch re-threw, and the wrapped envelope ended up in a toast.',
