      'Root cause: in v0.23.0 I bound onPointerMove + onPointerUp to BOTH the resize handles AND the element wrapper. With pointer capture on the handle, the browser fires the event on the handle — fine — but React then bubbles the synthetic event up to ancestor handlers. The wrapper\'s handler fired second with the wrong reference.',
      'Fix: pointer capture and ALL move/up handlers live on the WRAPPER now, for every drag mode (body move, 8-handle resize, rotation knob). Handle and knob only have onPointerDown — they\'re just trigger points; the wrapper owns the drag. Single canvas-reference resolution: `wrapper.parentElement = canvas`, no mode-dependent traversal.',
