      'Fix: a 2000×2000 (square) template was rendering as a rectangle in the editor canvas. The CSS used `width: 100% + max-height: 100% + aspect-ratio: 1 / 1` together, which is a known bad combo — width filled the column\'s full width, max-height clamped the height, and the aspect-ratio constraint silently broke. The canvas became "column width × column height" regardless of the template\'s ratio.',
      'Replaced with JS-driven sizing. EditorCanvas now measures the wrap\'s available area via ResizeObserver, picks the smaller of (availW, availH × aspect) or (availH, availW ÷ aspect), and applies the result as inline width/height on the canvas div. Classic letterbox fit — whichever dimension is the limiter drives the size, the other follows from the template\'s ratio.',
