      'Why JS instead of fixing the CSS: I tried `aspect-ratio + max-width: 100% + max-height: 100%` (no explicit width / height). It collapses to 0 in a flex column because there\'s no preferred dimension. The CSS approach that "just works" would be using a sized parent + display:grid + place-items:center + max-width / max-height — but that\'s more rework than a 6-line ResizeObserver effect. JS sizing is also more honest about what the canvas should be.',
