      'Undo / Redo: press Cmd+Z to undo, Cmd+Shift+Z to redo. Visible "↶ Undo" / "↷ Redo" buttons in the editor toolbar with disabled states so you can see when there\'s history available. The history holds up to 50 entries and is session-local (closes when you leave the editor, but every saved state still persists via the normal save path).',
      'History uses a "settle-commit" pattern: after any template change, a 300ms timer waits to see if more changes are coming; if it stays quiet, the PREVIOUS state goes into the past stack. That naturally captures end-of-drag and end-of-keystroke as one history entry instead of fifty (one per pixel of drag). The trade-off is a small commit delay — if you Cmd+Z immediately after releasing a drag, the checkpoint might still be in the 300ms settle window. Wait half a second and it works.',
