      'Fix: v0.22.8 still left some thumbnails stale for users on older libraries. The cache-bust fallback was `contentHash || filepath` — but the filepath is exactly what gets recycled across rows after the server renumbers files on disk. For images imported before v0.10.x (when content_hash was added) the column is null, so the fallback to filepath made the cache key still the same after delete. Fixed: now `contentHash || image.id || filepath`. The row id is stable and unique per row identity, so the URL ?v=<id> differs between the deleted row and the surviving row that takes its filepath slot — even without a content hash.',
      'New: explicit "Removed `<filename>`" success toast after deleting a product image. Now you get THREE visual confirmations of what just happened: (1) the confirm modal told you which filename you\'re about to delete, (2) the toast names the file that was just removed, (3) the tile actually disappears from its position (this part already worked in v0.22.8 via id-based React keying).',
