      'Root cause: the server renumbers files on disk after every image delete/reorder/set-main so they stay contiguous (001..NNN). The browser caches thumbnails by URL. Path `<sku>-003.jpg` stayed the same URL but the bytes inside changed — so the browser served the previous image\'s pixels for that slot. Combined with React keying tiles by filepath (which all stayed the same too), the only visible "removed" tile was the trailing one that fell off the end of the list.',
      'Three fixes layered together:',
      '(1) ImageTile + ImageStrip thumbs now key by row id, not filepath. Row id is stable through renames; filepath is not. React now correctly removes the DOM node for the actually-deleted image.',
      '(2) Every `app-image://local/<path>` URL now includes a `?v=<contentHash>` cache-bust query parameter. Same bytes → same hash → same URL → cache hit (fast). Different bytes after renumber → different hash → fresh fetch. The protocol handler at main/protocol.js already supported `?v=...` (it strips the querystring before resolving on disk), so this is just the renderer adopting it.',
      '(3) Server now bumps the parent product\'s `updated_at` on every image event (add, remove, reorder, set-main). The Library list + grid thumbnails use `?v=<updatedAt>` since they don\'t have a content hash on hand — so the product table thumb also refreshes after image changes.',
